10195	{"artifactId":"LLD-babd84c6e2fb480a-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-babd84c6e2fb480a-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-15T05:29:10.330Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The reviewer's feedback (opened files follow the same placement as the review-pane placement fix) is designed: open-code-ref takes its viewColumn from the existing reviewColumn closure (chooseReviewColumn), falling back to Beside, never the chat group.","evidence":"extension.ts:717-725 defines `const reviewColumn = (): vscode.ViewColumn | undefined => { ... return chooseReviewColumn(groups, CHAT_VIEW_TYPE) ... }`, and createPanel at :733-736 uses `column ?? vscode.ViewColumn.Beside` when quiet. The LLD's migration step 2, its edge-case row and its integration test 'opens a clicked code reference in the column chooseReviewColumn picks, and Beside when it picks none' all reuse that rule. One caveat: reviewColumn is declared at :717, after `const chatHost = createChatPanelHost({` at :611, inside the same `if (chatEnabled)` block. The chat host's open-file dependency must read it lazily from inside a lambda, or the declaration must move above :611. Building it as written works if the lambda is only called after activation. [files: vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts]","action":"none; the implementer should declare reviewColumn before createChatPanelHost, or reference it only inside the dependency lambda","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"There is no upstream SPEC or acceptance criteria; ac1-ac3 are derived from the Story's user-value points, and no non-goal is built.","evidence":"The standalone directory docs/standalone/make-links-code-references-clickable-chat-E20261015babd84c6/ contains only S001/LLD.md, with no SPEC or ISSUE. Open question 1 states the derivation openly. The chosen design builds nothing beyond linking http(s) and code references on the two surfaces.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"guardMd today keeps http(s) hrefs and sets rel=noopener noreferrer and target=_blank, removes every other href, and strips img src/srcset. The same text is carried in render-registry.ts and docs-review-panel.ts.","evidence":"render-registry.ts:421-424 and docs-review-panel.ts:125-128 are identical: `if(/^https?:/i.test(hr)){as[i].setAttribute('rel','noopener noreferrer');as[i].setAttribute('target','_blank');}else{as[i].removeAttribute('href');}` and then `ig[j].removeAttribute('src');ig[j].removeAttribute('srcset')`. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/render-registry.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-panel.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"chat-panel.ts and docs-review-panel.ts do not import vscode, so the open dependencies must be injected from extension.ts.","evidence":"A grep for `from 'vscode'` / `import * as vscode` in chat-panel.ts, docs-review-panel.ts and companion-reader.ts found nothing. extension.ts injects `open: (path) => ... executeCommand('vscode.open', vscode.Uri.file(path))` (around :616) and `readCompanion: createCompanionReader(...)` (:763). [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-panel.ts, vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"resolveWithin can be extracted from companion-reader.ts: containment is checked on the path as written and again after realpath, and createCompanionReader keeps its docs/ root, .html and size-cap rules.","evidence":"companion-reader.ts:28-31 has a private `within(dir, path)`. Lines :39-49 check `isAbsolute(relPath)`, then `within(docs, file)`, then `realpath` on both and `within(realDocs, realFile)`, then `stat.isFile() && size <= COMPANION_MAX_BYTES`. That is exactly the realpath-based symlink refusal the LLD's error path describes. No exported resolveWithin exists today, so calling it new is correct. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/companion-reader.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The vscode.d.ts shim lacks env.openExternal, Range and Position, so it must gain them.","evidence":"vscode.d.ts:165-170: `export namespace env { export const appName: string; export const uriScheme: string; }`. It has no openExternal, and a grep found no `class Range` or `class Position` in the shim. [files: vscode-plugin/src/vscode.d.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Adding open-link and open-code-ref to the WebviewToHost union and to WEBVIEW_TO_HOST_TYPES, next to open-attachment and open-companion, is the full protocol change.","evidence":"protocol.ts:262 and :302 declare the open-companion and open-attachment variants, and :333-356 lists WEBVIEW_TO_HOST_TYPES. Outside tests that list is used only as a type and in the protocol tests, not as a runtime filter. Both hosts dispatch with `switch (msg.type)` and a `default:` that accepts and ignores (chat-panel.ts:2030, docs-review-panel.ts:2345), so new cases are added there. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/protocol.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-panel.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Tests that pin the scrub and the shell are found and updated: docs-review-panel.test.ts t4 (the https href keeps rel and target), the SHELL_BASELINE pins, the verbatim-once inline test, and the render-registry innerHTML+guardMd pairing assertion.","evidence":"docs-review-panel.test.ts:615 is 't4: guardMd strips a non-http href and an image src', with a `safe` https anchor. SHELL_BASELINE at :1245 is asserted at :1271-1272, :3949, :6002-6004 and :7080. :3968 is 'the shell inlines each of its source strings verbatim and exactly once', over DOCS_BODY_RENDERER_SOURCE and others. Putting the linkify inside the renderer source keeps that test true. render-registry.test.ts:196 and :428 assert `/\\.innerHTML=[^;]*;guardMd\\(/`; linkify after guardMd keeps that pairing. The regex pins in review-wiring.test.ts:176-181 and extension-chat-wiring.test.ts:326 match the existing text and still hold if the change only adds code. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/docs-review-panel.test.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/render-registry.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"No stored data changes: the new messages only add to the protocol, and an older page that never sends them is unaffected.","evidence":"Both hosts' switch statements accept and ignore unknown types in `default:` (chat-panel.ts:2030-2033, docs-review-panel.ts:2345-2347), so adding variants changes the meaning of no existing message. Nothing is persisted: the transcript keeps the raw markdown, and linkify runs at render time. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-panel.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every failure on the host side is caught and logged, never thrown into the message handler. This matches the existing open-attachment handling.","evidence":"chat-panel.ts:2018-2028 already wraps `att.open(ref.path)` in try/catch with `log.warn`, and extension.ts wraps vscode.open in a promise rejection handler. The LLD states detection and response for six cases: non-http url, an escaping path (realpath compare, as in companion-reader.ts:45-47), a missing file, no workspace folder, a vscode.open rejection, and openExternal rejecting or returning false. Each case can be detected with the stated mechanism. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/companion-reader.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every derived criterion (ac1 http, ac2 code refs plus placement, ac3 both surfaces plus guardMd invariant) maps to named tests. The placement rule from the feedback has its own integration test.","evidence":"The acceptance-mapping table names tests for ac1-ac3. ac2 includes 'the host opens a clicked code reference in the column chooseReviewColumn picks, and Beside when it picks none'. ac3 includes a renderer-source test run against a stub DOM, which follows this repo's run-it-not-grep-it convention for DOCS_BODY_RENDERER_SOURCE (docs-review-panel.ts:105-110, loadRenderer in the test file :561-566). Whether VS Code opens the link only once and places the file in the chosen group can only be checked live; the LLD lists both as open questions to confirm by hand. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/docs-review-panel.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":11,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-15T05:29:10.330Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
